WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.880
we started working with Home Service Studios and

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.360
those guys are great and uh,

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.360
not only just on the business end of

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.320
it, but um, we've created some valuable friendships

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.080
out of it as well.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.960
and we've just gained a lot of awareness

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.799
in the community. It's it's one of those

00:00:16.799 --> 00:00:18.480
things I I don't really like being on

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.080
camera. I'm not flashy.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.760
I'm not the guy that's out there,

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.760
you know, on on Instagram and just saying,

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:24.960
"Hey, look at what I'm doing.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.120
Look at this. Look at that." Um I'm

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.080
just kind of in the background uh watching.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.000
And so it's a little more out of

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.919
out of my comfort zone to to do

00:00:33.919 --> 00:00:36.159
this. But I knew going into it,

00:00:36.159 --> 00:00:37.440
this is where we need to go to

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.039
get our brand out there.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:41.440
And so we kind of stepped into that

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.320
uncomfortable territory and started doing it.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:45.600
We started getting a lot of good feedback.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.600
We would we would get to the customer's

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.519
home and it was like they already made

00:00:49.519 --> 00:00:50.799
their mind up that they were going to

00:00:50.799 --> 00:00:52.240
purchase from us cuz they were like,

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.159
"Oh, we already seen all your videos.

00:00:54.159 --> 00:00:56.960
We you know, we we read your reviews.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.000
What's there to do?" It's like,

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.279
"Oh, well, we we still got to get

00:00:59.279 --> 00:01:00.960
you a price. Yeah.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.399
We still got to run through our process."

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:04.320
So that's been really huge.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.840
And it's also been really huge in recruiting.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.919
Yeah, because the technicians or whoever you might

00:01:11.919 --> 00:01:14.720
be trying to recruit feels like they already

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.079
know the company. Uh they got a little

00:01:17.079 --> 00:01:19.520
inside into the company and how you run

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.800
and your culture and uh they feel comfortable

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.200
making that jump because that's a big commitment

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.960
especially in a small town where there's not

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.639
many options. Uh you can burn bridges really

00:01:29.639 --> 00:01:31.599
quick. They want to make sure that they're

00:01:31.599 --> 00:01:32.960
making the right moves as well.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:33.000
Well, you know,
